WEBVTT

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:05.165
Welcome to Alaventra. Rank in
search. Get recommended by AI.

00:00:06.143 --> 00:00:11.693
In tutorial 11.6, you'll make sure
everyone in your company signs in safely,

00:00:11.743 --> 00:00:14.508
through your own identity
provider if you have one.

00:00:15.519 --> 00:00:18.658
First, open Company settings,
and choose Security.

00:00:21.473 --> 00:00:25.348
If you see this note, turn on
two-step for your own account first,

00:00:25.398 --> 00:00:28.029
as shown in tutorial 11.5.

00:00:29.003 --> 00:00:32.228
Then switch on Require
two-step verification.

00:00:32.278 --> 00:00:35.986
Members without it see nothing of
this company until they set it up.

00:00:37.035 --> 00:00:41.770
Sign-ins through single sign-on, or a Google
Workspace that asks for a second step,

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:44.302
can count too. Then click Save.

00:00:45.296 --> 00:00:49.981
Below, Who has two-step verification
shows who still needs to set it up.

00:00:50.031 --> 00:00:52.033
Show me how gives you
a guide to send them.

00:00:53.046 --> 00:00:57.621
Next, under Sessions and records,
choose when idle members are signed out,

00:00:57.671 --> 00:01:00.206
and how long the audit
log keeps what happened.

00:01:01.205 --> 00:01:05.155
Now open Single sign-on.
Under Your e-mail domains,

00:01:05.205 --> 00:01:09.037
type the part after the at sign in
your team's addresses, and click Add.

00:01:10.067 --> 00:01:14.417
Add the record it shows where you manage
your domain, then click Check now.

00:01:14.467 --> 00:01:18.796
Once it's proven, a domain shows as
Verified, like the first one here.

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:23.995
Under Identity provider,
choose OpenID Connect or SAML,

00:01:24.045 --> 00:01:28.470
whichever your provider uses. Copy
these values into your provider,

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:30.714
and paste in the details it gives you.

00:01:31.709 --> 00:01:35.534
Choose whether people join at their
first sign-in, and with which role.

00:01:35.584 --> 00:01:37.913
Click Save, and then Test sign-in.

00:01:39.188 --> 00:01:42.288
After a good test, single sign-on is on.

00:01:42.338 --> 00:01:47.152
Require single sign-on makes it the only
way in, while owners keep their password.

00:01:48.111 --> 00:01:51.396
With Provisioning, copy the
address and create a token,

00:01:51.446 --> 00:01:56.301
a private key for your provider, so it
can add people, map its groups to roles,

00:01:56.351 --> 00:01:57.769
and switch people off.

00:01:58.806 --> 00:02:04.456
Finally, open Audit log. Every sign-in,
team change and settings change is listed,

00:02:04.506 --> 00:02:06.215
and nothing in it can be edited.

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:10.320
Filter by what, who, outcome or dates,

00:02:10.370 --> 00:02:13.748
and click Export CSV to share
it with your security team.

00:02:14.758 --> 00:02:18.183
Now everyone in your company
signs in with a second step,

00:02:18.233 --> 00:02:20.478
and you can show exactly who did what.

00:02:21.487 --> 00:02:25.462
So, require two-step, set your
time limits, prove your domain,

00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:29.355
connect your provider, turn on
provisioning, and check the audit log.

00:02:30.318 --> 00:02:35.818
Everyone signs in safely. Next, run
your clients from one agency workspace,

00:02:35.868 --> 00:02:38.004
in tutorial 11.7.
